Dogs are loyal and intelligent animals that have lived alongside humans for thousands of years. They are known for their companionship, protective nature, and ability to learn commands and tasks quickly. Dogs come in many breeds, sizes, and personalities, ranging from small lap dogs to large working dogs used in rescue, security, and farming activities. They are often called “man’s best friend” because of their strong bond with people and their affectionate behavior. Dogs also play important roles in society as service animals, therapy companions, police dogs, and family pets.